Binary source availability

Runnable CMake builds include source/afterlight-source.zip alongside this
notice (inside Contents/Resources on macOS). Extract it to obtain the covered
Afterlight source, including build scripts, shaders, sample game modules and
local modifications present when the binary was built. The source is available
under MPL-2.0, except for the identified third-party material under its own terms.
Build instructions are in the archive's README.md. No additional charge applies.

Exports preserve that archive and these notices. Generated starter modules also
include source/game-source.zip with their marked MPL source and modifications.
Independent game files can have their own license; copying or modifying an MPL
template creates covered source. Additional custom covered modules must be
accompanied by their corresponding source; see docs/licensing.md.

Keep the corresponding source and notices available with binary distributions.
Any additional binary/game terms must preserve recipients' MPL source rights.
